    "id": "richfrem/agent-plugins-skills/os-lab-log",
    "name": "os-lab-log",
    "description": "Persistent, append-only log of Skill Improvement Lab runs plus the charts and progress report built from it. Appends a dated entry to context/experiment-log/ after a run, queries past runs by keyword, prints aggregate summary counts, and renders the improvement trend chart (KEEP/DISCARD dots, running-best line) with generate_report.py. Use after any lab run to persist results before temp/ is cleared, and to answer \"are we getting better?\". Trigger phrases: \"log this run\", \"append to the experiment log\", \"query the experiment log\", \"summarize all experiment runs\", \"show me the improvement chart\", \"progress report\", \"graph the eval scores\", \"what's the trend\". DO NOT USE to run the improvement loop (use os-lab-loop), to score one skill change (use os-lab-scorer), to review or backport a lab diff (use os-lab-backport), or to write session memory (use os-lab-memory).\n",
